{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["And the reason for <b>\"But Noah found favor in the eyes of HaShem\"</b> is that all his deeds were pleasant and pleasing before Him. Similarly, \"For you have found favor in My eyes, and I have known you by name\" (Exodus 33:17), in the manner of \"And he gave him favor in the eyes of the officer of the prison\" (Genesis 39:21), \"And Esther found favor in the eyes of all who saw her\" (Esther 2:15). And He mentioned this in contrast to what He said about his generation, that all their deeds were a source of grief before Him, may He be blessed, and He said about him that he was a source of favor in His eyes. Afterward He explained why he was good in the eyes of Elohim: because he was a righteous man, wholehearted."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:25:24.619195103Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}